This license covers my own work in this repository: Ishido for Windows
(1993-1995) and what I added in 2026 (the tools, the documentation, the
screenshots and recordings). It does not cover:

- release/BWCC.DLL (also the 1995 version used for the recordings, which is
  not in the repository): Borland's Windows Custom Controls library,
  (c) Borland International.
- source/ISHIDO.PAS: the program skeleton of an article in the magazine
  WinDOS, on which I built the first version in 1993. I do not remember
  the article, I could not find it, and I do not know how much of its code
  or its ideas are left; if any, they remain with their author or
  publisher.
- release/ISHIDO.EXE contains the run-time library and ObjectWindows of
  Borland Pascal, (c) Borland International.
- source/WINDOS.BMP: the logo of the magazine WinDOS.
- source/STONES.BMP and the same sheet inside source/ISHIDO.RES: the 36
  stone pictures. I do not remember who drew them; they may not be my own
  work. The logo and the banner (also in ISHIDO.RES) are mine.

The game Ishido was designed by Michael Feinberg and published by
Accolade; this is an unofficial version. The names of the games, magazines
and products mentioned belong to their respective owners.
